From 7d36198bf7367e2726c31994ccf9e78fb75a72e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:33:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 130/132] power: supply: bq256xx: Charge at the battery's
 constant charge current

The driver reads the battery's constant-charge-current-max-microamp,
takes it as the most the charge current may be set to, and then
programs the chip's default fast charge current anyway: a BQ25601 with
a battery rated for 3 A charges at 2.04 A until userspace raises it.

Program the battery's value instead. Without battery information that
value is the chip's default, as before.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
index 98540b1..736cb7f 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
@@ -1639,8 +1639,12 @@ static int bq256xx_hw_init(struct bq256xx_device *bq)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Charge at the battery's own constant charge current: the chip's
+	 * default is what bat_info holds when the battery says nothing.
+	 */
 	ret = bq->chip_info->bq256xx_set_ichg(bq,
-				bq->chip_info->bq256xx_def_ichg);
+				bat_info->constant_charge_current_max_ua);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
